    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can offer personalized explanations, adapt to different learning speeds, and provide instant feedback. They can break down tough topics into simple steps, like baking or hiking. Students can ask questions anytime, and get clear, friendly answers. This makes learning less intimidating and more accessible, especially for those who didn’t get strong foundations early on."
